UPDATE companies SET description='Bluegrass Superior Foods, LLC operates from Louisville, Kentucky. The company was founded with a mission to serve others through quality food products, though the exact founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed.

The company functions as a national full-service contract and private label packer for the food industry. Its services span product development, packaging, and labeling compliance, with capabilities to produce a wide range of wet and dry items including spices, rubs, breading, hot sauces, barbecue sauces, salad dressings, syrups, juice drinks, marinades, jams, jellies, and pie fillings. The firm emphasizes flexibility, accepting projects of any size without minimum order requirements.

Bluegrass Superior Foods serves a broad spectrum of food-industry clients, from startup entrepreneurs developing their first product to established brands seeking co-packing support. The company is a member of the Kentucky Proud program and produces goods for other Kentucky Proud members, highlighting its regional ties.

The company states its purpose is to maintain a safe, injury-free workplace while manufacturing food that meets the highest safety and quality standards. It aims to minimize environmental impact, comply with all relevant regulations, and offer competitive pricing. A stated differentiator is the willingness to handle orders of any quantity, distinguishing it from co-packers that impose large minimums.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Contract packing", "Private label packing", "Product development", "Packaging", "Labeling and compliance", "Organic certification (USDA National Organic Program)", "FDA acidified food manufacturing", "Shelf-stable food manufacturing", "Recipe development", "Regulatory compliance assistance"], "industries": ["Food industry", "Food and beverage", "Kentucky Proud program"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["No minimum order quantities", "Certified Organic under US National Organic Program", "FDA compliance for acidified and shelf-stable foods", "Kentucky Proud member", "Product development and regulatory compliance support"], "facts_used": ["Location: Louisville, Kentucky -> db", "Mission: passion to serve others with quality and superior products -> /", "Contract and private label packer -> /services", "Product development, packaging, labeling & compliance services -> /services", "Product variety: spices, rubs, breading, hot sauces, BBQ sauces, salad dressings, syrup, juice drinks, marinades, jams, jellies, pie fillings -> /services", "No minimum order quantities -> /services", "Certified Organic under US National Organic Program -> /services", "FDA compliance for acidified and shelf-stable foods -> /services", "Kentucky Proud member -> /services", "Mission: safe, injury-free, friendly, healthy workplace -> /", "Minimize environmental impact -> /", "Highest standards, quality ingredients, regulatory compliance -> /", "Competitive and affordable prices -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Bluegrass Superior Foods is a national full-service contract and private label packer serving a wide range of client-partners in the food industry.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "Any quantity (no minimum)", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='bluegrass-superior-foods-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Bluejay Diagnostics, Inc. was founded in 2015 in Acton, Massachusetts. The company is publicly traded on the NASDAQ under the ticker BJDX.

Bluejay is a late-stage, pre-revenue medical device company developing the Symphony™ Suite, a near-patient testing system designed to deliver sample-to-result measurements in approximately 20 minutes. Its first product candidate is an IL-6 test cartridge for sepsis triage, intended for use in hospital and long-term acute care settings. The company is currently conducting the SYMON-II pivotal clinical trial, which completed enrollment of 624 patients in early 2026, and anticipates submitting for FDA approval in 2027.

By moving testing out of the central laboratory and to the patient bedside, the system aims to accelerate treatment decisions for conditions such as sepsis, where early intervention is critical.

