UPDATE companies SET description='Buitoni Food Company is headquartered in Danville, Virginia, but its roots trace back to 1827 in Sansepolcro, Tuscany, where Giulia Buitoni founded the business after trading her necklace for a pasta machine. The company began as a small artisan pasta maker, sourcing wheat from Puglia and building a reputation for quality that eventually attracted royal attention.

Today, Buitoni produces fresh pasta, sauces, and cheeses using artisan techniques. Its processes include pasta making with imported 00 flour from Italy, slow-roasting chicken for fillings, and a selective process for aged DOP Parmigiano Reggiano. The company also uses farm-fresh eggs. Specific facility size, headcount, and production volumes are not disclosed.

