UPDATE companies SET description='Cablecraft Motion Controls is headquartered in St. Matthews, South Carolina. The company traces its origins to 1949 when Cablecraft was founded in Tacoma, Washington, to manufacture aircraft cable assemblies. Earlier roots go back to 1920 with J.J. Tourek Manufacturing Co. in Chicago producing precision screw-machine components, and 1954 with Superior Ball Joint Corp. in Fort Wayne, Indiana. The current entity emerged from a combination of Cable Manufacturing & Assembly and Cablecraft into a global leader in engineered motion controls.

The company designs and manufactures control cables (push and push-pull), rod ends, ball joints, mechanical linkages, and remote actuation products. It also produces mechatronic assemblies including electronic controls and electro-mechanical components. Cablecraft''s engineering team develops proprietary components to reduce design time and tooling costs, and offers custom component design per proprietary requirements. The firm operates a worldwide cable assembler network and provides engineering collaboration from concept to installation-ready delivery.

Cablecraft serves aerospace (sport aircraft), powersports (throttle and shift assemblies), construction (heavy-duty high-temperature applications), automotive (light vehicles), and industrial engine controls. The company''s application engineers work directly with client technical teams to adapt standard products or develop new designs.

