UPDATE companies SET description='Cal-Maine Foods, Inc. was founded in 1957 by Fred R. Adams, Jr. in Jackson, Mississippi. The company is headquartered in Ridgeland, Mississippi, and has been publicly traded on NASDAQ under the ticker CALM since 1996. It began as a single egg operation and grew through a series of mergers and acquisitions, including the 1969 merger of Adams Foods with Dairy Fresh Products and Maine Egg Farms to form Cal-Maine Foods.

The company produces a full range of egg products, from conventional and cage-free shell eggs to organic, free-range, pasture-raised, and nutritionally enhanced specialty eggs, as well as prepared egg-based foods such as ready-to-eat egg products and breakfast foods. The company maintains approximately 50 million laying hens and sold 1.2 billion dozen eggs in fiscal 2026, generating $2.9 billion in net sales.

Cal-Maine Foods serves retail and foodservice channels nationwide under brands including Eggland''s Best, Land O'' Lakes, Farmhouse Eggs, Crepini, and Van''s Foods. Its customers range from household consumers to foodservice operators and retail chains across the United States.

The company states its purpose is to be the consumer-driven provider of nutritious, affordable, and sustainable eggs and egg-based foods that fit today''s lifestyles. It emphasizes a disciplined acquisition strategy — integrating 26 companies since 1989 — and commitments to sustainable operations, strong corporate governance, and community support.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Shell egg production (conventional, cage-free, organic, free-range, pasture-raised, nutritionally enhanced)", "Prepared egg product manufacturing (ready-to-eat, hard-cooked, breakfast foods)", "Egg processing and packaging", "Feed milling", "Pullet growing", "Breeding and hatchery operations", "Food manufacturing (prepared foods)", "Joint venture management", "Acquisition integration"], "industries": ["Food manufacturing", "Retail", "Foodservice", "Agriculture (egg production)"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "1.2 billion dozen eggs annually (fiscal 2026)", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Largest U.S. egg producer with approximately 50 million laying hens", "Full product portfolio from conventional to specialty and prepared egg foods", "Nationwide network of 51 shell egg production and 5 food manufacturing facilities", "Disciplined acquisition strategy integrating 26 companies since 1989", "Publicly traded (NASDAQ: CALM) with $2.9 billion annual net sales"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1957 by Fred R. Adams, Jr. in Jackson, Mississippi -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Ridgeland, Mississippi -> /about-us", "Publicly traded on NASDAQ (CALM) since 1996 -> db", "Largest egg company in the United States -> /about-us", "50 million laying hens, $2.9B annual net sales, 1.2B dozen eggs sold annually (fiscal 2026) -> /", "Facility counts as of May 30, 2026: 2 breeding, 2 hatcheries, 29 feed mills, 51 shell egg production, 38 pullet, 52 processing/packaging, 5 food manufacturing -> /about-us", "Product range: conventional, cage-free, organic,