UPDATE companies SET description='Capital Electro Circuits Inc., based in Gaithersburg, Maryland, has been manufacturing printed circuit boards since 1985.

The shop produces rigid, flexible, and rigid‑flex boards with capabilities that include multilayer constructions up to 16 layers, finished thicknesses up to 1.300 inches, copper weights up to 6 oz outer/4 oz inner, and advanced features such as blind/buried vias, edge plating, and castellations. Materials span standard FR‑4 and high‑Tg laminates, polyimides, and a wide range of RF/microwave substrates from Rogers, Arlon, Taconic, and TMM/Teflon families. In‑house services cover CAM with DFM analysis, CNC routing and milling, electrical testing, and a full suite of surface finishes including HASL, ENIG, ENEPIG, immersion tin/silver, and hard gold.

The company serves aerospace and defense (supplying 100 % U.S.-made boards for military and avionics programs), medical and healthcare (precision boards for imaging and diagnostic equipment), telecommunications (high‑frequency circuits for 5G and satellite), automotive and EV (durable boards for electric and autonomous vehicles), and RF/microwave applications. Named customers include Northrop Grumman, BAE Systems, NASA, Lockheed Martin, Honeywell, Sandia National Laboratories, Booz Allen Hamilton, and the U.S. Army.

Capital Electro Circuits positions itself as a specialty fabricator that takes on jobs outside standard PCB lines, often developing custom processes for unique designs. Its stated mission is to support what the customer requires, not only what they ask for, and it maintains a conflict‑minerals sourcing policy with vetted vendors and full CMRT disclosure.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','UL 94V-0','RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Rigid PCB fabrication", "Flexible PCB fabrication", "Rigid-flex PCB fabrication", "Multilayer PCB (up to 16 layers)", "Thick PCB fabrication (up to 1.300\")", "Blind/buried vias", "Edge plating", "Castellations", "High-frequency/RF microwave PCB", "Thermal management PCBs (aluminum-backed)", "CNC routing and milling", "In-house electrical testing", "CAM/DFM services", "Controlled impedance", "Surface finishes: HASL, ENIG, ENEPIG, immersion tin/silver, hard gold", "LPI solder mask", "Legend printing", "Panel routing and scoring", "Blanket orders and split deliveries", "Subcontracting for design and assembly", "Conflict minerals compliance"], "industries": ["Aerospace & Defense", "Medical & Healthcare", "Telecommunications", "Automotive & EVs", "RF & Microwave Applications"], "materials": ["FR-4", "FR-406", "FR-408", "BT", "Polyimides", "GETEK", "Rogers Corporation/Arlon 3000/4000/5000/6000 series", "Arlon CuClad, DiClad, AD series", "Non-Woven and Woven PTFE", "RO4000, RO4350", "TMM3, TMM4, TMM6, TMM10, TMM10I", "Taconic Microwave Materials (TLY, TLX, TLE, TLC, TLT, RF-35)", "IsoClad 900 Series", "Ceramic Filled PTFE", "Aluminum/Brass/Copper Heat Sink Circuits", "Thermasil bonding film"], "equipment": ["CAM station", "CNC routing and milling equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "Machining \u00b10.005 in down to \u00b10.001 in; registration \u00b10.002 in; controlled impedance \u00b110%; thickness \u00b110%", "built_on": ["100% USA-based PCB manufacturing for military and avionics", "Specialty fabricatio