UPDATE companies SET description='Capitol Iron Works operates from Gaithersburg, Maryland, in the heart of the DC–Maryland–Virginia corridor. The company was founded in August 2014 by Ronald Vargas, who immigrated from Nicaragua in 2004 and learned welding as a helper at Bethesda Iron Works before earning his certification and launching his own shop, initially called Capitol Iron Solutions. Vargas serves as president and co‑owner.

The shop produces custom ornamental and architectural metalwork in ferrous and non‑ferrous metals — stainless steel, aluminum, bronze, structural steel, wrought iron, and glass. Core processes include welding, cutting, shaping, decorative detailing, powder‑coat finishing, and on‑site installation. The facility has expanded from a 1,100‑square‑foot space with a single fabrication bay to a 4,300‑square‑foot plant housing three fabrication units, staffed by 14 employees. Project sizes range from $1,000 residential railings to $500,000 commercial installations, with 2018 revenue projected at $1.5 million.

Capitol Iron Works serves residential, commercial, and government clients across the DMV. Notable government work includes bronze railing fabrication and installation for the Architect of the Capitol at the Rayburn House Office Building. The company also works with architects, contractors, and property owners in cities such as Bethesda, Rockville, Alexandria, and Arlington.

Vargas attributes the firm’s rapid growth to two factors: a loyal, low‑turnover team (only one departure in four years) and a willingness to tackle technically difficult, intricate projects that other shops decline. He emphasizes on‑schedule delivery, direct communication, and a single‑source approach from design through installation.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom ornamental metalwork", "Architectural railing fabrication", "Stair and handrail fabrication", "Glass railing fabrication", "Cable railing fabrication", "Steel fencing fabrication", "Balcony fabrication", "Canopy fabrication", "Automatic gate fabrication", "Structural welding", "Custom welding & fabrication", "Metal cutting and shaping", "Decorative metal detailing", "Powder coating", "On-site installation", "Restoration of existing metalwork"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Government"], "materials": ["Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Bronze", "Structural steel", "Wrought iron", "Glass"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Project values from $1,000 to $500,000", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Customer\u2011service\u2011first approach with direct communication and on\u2011time delivery", "Low employee turnover \u2014 only one departure in the first four years", "Full in\u2011house capability from design and fabrication through installation and restoration", "Willingness to accept complex, intricate ornamental and architectural metalwork", "Single\u2011source responsibility for both ferrous and non\u2011ferrous projects"], "facts_used": ["Founded August 2014 by Ronald Vargas -> /about-us", "Facility grew from 1,100 to 4,300 sq ft with three fabrication units -> /about-us", "Employee count 14 -> /about-us", "Project range $1,000 to $500,000 -> /about-us", "Government client: Architect of the Capitol (Rayburn House Office Building) -> /about-us", "Materials: stainless steel, aluminum, bronze, structural steel, wrought iron, glass -> /about-us and 