UPDATE companies SET description='Carolina CoverTech operates from North Augusta, South Carolina, where it runs a U.S.-based contract manufacturing operation focused on RF welding, heat sealing, and precision industrial sewing. The company does not publicly disclose its founding year or ownership structure, but it presents itself as a partner for custom fabric-based product development and production.

The shop’s core capabilities center on RF welding and heat sealing for precise seals, industrial sewing across a range of materials, and a product development cycle that moves from rapid prototyping through process validation to full-scale production. It also offers rigid-to-flexible conversions, turning rigid components into lighter, more versatile fabric alternatives. Outputs include flexible protective covers, bladders, industrial containers, and custom bags, with the company citing a portfolio of thousands of completed projects.

While the firm states it serves “all industries,” its published case work highlights military and defense fabrication for Department of Defense contractors and prime suppliers, including tactical pouches, load-bearing equipment, and protective enclosures. A blog post on NFPA 701 certified fabric requirements further suggests involvement in commercial and institutional markets where flame-resistant hanging textiles are specified.

Carolina CoverTech frames its differentiation around a stated mission “to make life better for our customers, team members, trade partners and the community,” backed by values of excellence, customer-centeredness, innovation, selfless ownership, and stewardship. Its four-step process — discovery, prototype, process, and shipping — is designed to move from concept to delivery with a commitment to respond to inquiries within one business day.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["RF welding", "Heat sealing", "Industrial sewing", "Product development", "Rapid prototyping (fabric products)", "Rigid-to-flexible conversion", "Custom fabrication (cut, sew, seal)", "Flexible protective cover manufacturing", "Bladder manufacturing", "Industrial container manufacturing", "Custom bag manufacturing"], "industries": ["Military and defense (DoD contractors and prime suppliers)"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["RF welding and heat sealing for precise, repeatable seals", "Industrial sewing expertise across diverse material types", "End-to-end product development from rapid prototype to validated production process", "Rigid-to-flexible conversions that reduce weight, shipping cost, and manufacturing expense", "Four-step discovery-to-shipping process with a one-business-day inquiry response"], "facts_used": ["Location: North Augusta, SC -> /", "Business type: contract manufacturer specializing in RF welding, heat sealing, industrial sewing -> /", "Processes: RF welding, heat sealing, industrial sewing, product development, rapid prototyping, rigid-to-flexible conversion -> /", "Products: flexible protective covers, bladders, industrial containers, bags -> /", "Industries: military and defense for DoD contractors and prime suppliers -> / (blog post title)", "Mission and values: ''To Make Life Better...'' and five values -> /", "Process steps: Discovery, Prototype, Process, Shipping -> /", "Response time: respond within one business day -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db", "Phone and email -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Custom Contract Manufacturer Specializing in RF Welding/Heat Sealing and Precision Industrial Sewing", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/carolina-covertech/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='carolina-covertech' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Carolina Creative Products operates from Greenville, South Carolina, as a U.S.-based manufacturer of premium home soft goods. The company specializes in pillows, bedding, and fabric-based home products, focusing on repeatable, high-quality production that scales alongside the brands it serves.

Its capabilities span digital fabric printing through final cut-and-sew production, delivering integrated print-to-finish manufacturing for items such as decorative pillow covers, duvet covers, woven blankets, table linens, and pet beds. The facility emphasizes consistent color management, production built for repeat orders, and scalable manufacturing to support growing product lines, all under a domestic production model that reduces vendor complexity.

The company serves home and lifestyle brands developing repeatable collections, e-commerce brands transitioning to retail, designers and creative studios bringing original textile concepts to market, and hospitality and specialty programs requiring large-scale custom textile products. Carolina Creative Products positions itself as a long-term manufacturing partner rather than a one-off custom shop, supporting partners from initial sampling through ongoing production.

A stated differentiator is the company''s operation of its own home goods brand, Porch And Parlour, which provides firsthand insight into pricing, product development, fulfillment, and customer expectations. Leadership emphasizes that domestic manufacturing enables shorter lead times, greater flexibility, tighter quality control, reduced risk, improved communication, and protection of brand intellectual property, all supporting premium market positioning.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Digital fabric printing", "Cut-and-sew production", "Integrated print-to-finish production", "Color management", "Product development", "Quality control", "Domestic manufacturing", "Scalable production", "Repeat order fulfillment"], "industries": ["Home & Lifestyle Brands", "E-commerce Brands Scaling to Retail", "Designers & Creative Studios", "Hospitality & Specialty Programs", "Retail & Brand Programs"], "materials": ["Textiles", "Fabric"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Integrated print-to-finish production for tighter control and fewer handoffs", "Consistent color management across initial and repeat runs", "Production built for repeat orders and replenishment", "Scalable manufacturing to support growing product lines", "Domestic production for faster timelines and easier communication", "Operates own brand Porch And Parlour for firsthand market insight"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Greenville, South Carolina -> db", "Manufacturer of premium home soft goods specializing in pillows, bedding, fabric-based home products -> /about-us", "Offers digital fabric printing through final cut-and-sew production -> /", "Products include decorative pillow covers, duvet covers, woven blankets, table linens, pet beds -> /", "Capabilities: integrated print-to-finish production, consistent color management, production built for repeat orders, scalable manufacturing, domestic production for faster timelines, streaml