UPDATE companies SET description='Carolina Solar Energy (CSE) was founded in 2004 in Durham, North Carolina, by Richard Harkrader, an architect emeritus, building contractor, and solar installer. The family-owned business began with a goal to demonstrate that renewable energy legislation could build a solar industry in the state. After years of trial and error, Harkrader completed the first utility-scale solar project in the Southeast at NC State University in 2007. Business partner Gerry Dudzik joined that same year, bringing permitting experience from the cellular tower industry. In 2012, Richard''s daughter Carson Harkrader joined after a career at GE Energy, and she assumed leadership in 2018 when both founders retired.

The company develops utility-scale photovoltaic (PV) solar projects across the Southeast and Gulf South, with over 950 MWdc of projects operating or under construction. Its core services include site selection, interconnection applications, state permitting, landowner outreach, community relations, and policy advocacy. The team manages projects from early development through construction, collaborating with municipalities, utilities, and landowners. CSE also operates an intern program and has partnered with organizations like TROSA to provide workforce opportunities.

CSE serves utilities, municipal governments, and private landowners throughout North Carolina, Virginia, Kentucky, and Louisiana. Notable partners include the City of Raleigh, which completed its first major solar development with CSE, and Person County, which hosts three photovoltaic facilities totaling approximately five megawatts. The company focuses on bringing economic development to underserved areas and works with families who have managed land for generations.

CSE distinguishes itself through early-market entry and policy leadership. It was the first solar company to apply for Kentucky state-level permits in March 2020, and its advocacy work has helped shape renewable energy legislation in North Carolina. The firm emphasizes community acceptance, aiming to deliver projects that are welcomed by their host communities.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Utility-scale photovoltaic (PV) solar project development", "Site selection and project management", "Interconnection applications", "State permitting", "Landowner outreach and community relations", "Policy advocacy for renewable energy", "Municipal and utility collaboration", "Economic development for underserved areas", "Workforce development partnerships (e.g., TROSA)", "Intern program management"], "industries": ["Utility-scale solar energy", "Renewable energy", "Clean energy", "Photovoltaic solar energy", "Energy development", "Municipal government", "Utilities", "Landowner services"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Over 950 MWdc of projects operating or under construction", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["First utility-scale solar project in the Southeast (2007)", "First solar company to apply for Kentucky state-level permits (2020)", "Over 950 MWdc of projects operating or under construction", "Family-owned with multi-generational landowner relationships", "Policy advocacy leadership in NC renewable energy legislation"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2004 by Richard Harkrader -> /about", "First utility-scale solar project in Southeast at NC State in 2007 -> /about", "Over 950 MWdc of projects operating or under construction -> /", "Family-owned business -> / and /about", "Carson Harkrader became CEO in 2018 -> /about", "Projects in North Carolina, Virginia, Kentucky, Louisiana -> /about", "Partnership with City of Raleigh -> /", "Partnership with Person County -> /", "First to apply for Kentucky state-level permits in March 2020 -> /about", "Policy advocacy work with NC Sustainable Energy Association and Carolinas Clean Energy Business Association -> /about", "Team includes Carson Harkrader, Tyler Caron, Vann Joines, Benjamin Finch, Richard Harkrader -> /about"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We develop utility-scale photovoltaic (PV) solar energy projects across the Southeastern US.", "founded_year": "2004", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='carolina-solar-energy-iii-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Carolina Woodworks LLC operates from Lyman, South Carolina, in the Upstate region. The family-owned business draws on more than 30 years of hands-on woodworking experience passed through generations.

The company designs, builds, finishes, and installs fully custom cabinetry and architectural millwork. Its in-house shop produces kitchen cabinets, bathroom vanities, built-ins, entertainment centers, home office suites, and pantry systems. Work includes frameless, inset, face-frame, and partial-overlay construction, with dovetailed drawer boxes, BLUM soft-close hardware, and professional lacquer finishes applied on site.

Carolina Woodworks serves homeowners, custom home builders, remodelers, interior designers, and commercial clients throughout the Upstate. Projects range from single-room built-ins to whole-home cabinetry packages for new construction and renovation.

