UPDATE companies SET description='Carolina Yarn & Fabrics Inc operates from Laurens, South Carolina. The company traces its origins to 1984 when the ARMORFORM trade name was established for fabric-formed concrete revetments.

The company manufactures ARMORFORM fabric-formed concrete systems for erosion control, scour protection, and lining applications. Its process involves weaving double-layer geotextiles from polyester or nylon yarns, which serve as forms for casting high-strength, fine-aggregate concrete. The forms can be placed underwater or on dry land. The company also provides engineering support, project management, and field services.

Carolina Yarn & Fabrics serves engineering firms, government agencies, and commercial contractors across infrastructure, water management, environmental protection, industrial, and energy sectors. Notable projects include the Endicott Island installation inside the Arctic Circle, MSHA-approved mining applications, U.S. Navy underwater pipeline and cable protection, and the U.S. Army Corps of Engineers'' Olmsted Locks and Dam scour protection.

The company emphasizes engineered products backed by comprehensive technical support and responsive delivery, which it says drives repeat business from long-standing clients. It positions itself as a partner that assembles multidisciplinary teams to deliver sustainable solutions, focusing on meeting client expectations for delivery, innovation, quality, and service.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Fabric-formed concrete erosion control systems", "Fabric-formed concrete scour protection systems", "Fabric-formed concrete lining systems", "Double-layer woven geotextile manufacturing", "Polyester yarn weaving", "Nylon yarn weaving", "Concrete pumping and placement (underwater and dry land)", "Engineering and technical support", "Project management", "Field service management"], "industries": ["Engineering", "Government", "Commercial construction", "Infrastructure", "Water management", "Environmental protection", "Industrial", "Energy", "Mining", "Marine construction", "Hydraulic engineering"], "materials": ["Polyester yarn", "Nylon yarn", "Fine aggregate concrete", "Geotextiles"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Engineered products with comprehensive technical support", "Responsive delivery driving repeat business with long-standing clients", "Multidisciplinary teams of project managers, engineers, and field service managers", "Over 40 years of global ARMORFORM system installations", "Approvals from MSHA, U.S. Navy, and U.S. Army Corps of Engineers"], "facts_used": ["Company name: Carolina Yarn & Fabrics Inc -> db", "Headquarters: Laurens, South Carolina -> db", "Founded year: 1984 (ARMORFORM trade name established) -> page \"/\"", "Company type: Manufacturer -> db description", "Product: ARMORFORM fabric-formed concrete systems -> page \"/\"", "Process: Double-layer woven geotextiles from polyester/nylon yarns -> page \"/\"", "Installation: Underwater or dry land concrete placement -> page \"