UPDATE companies SET description='Carpenter Co. is headquartered in Moore, Oklahoma, and traces its origins to 1950 when it began as a local latex foam manufacturer.

Today, Carpenter operates more than 60 production locations worldwide and employs over 6,500 people. Its core manufacturing includes polyurethane foams, polyether polyols (a key component in flexible urethane foams), polyester fibers, and insulation materials. The company maintains state-of-the-art research and development facilities in Richmond and other sites, where expert teams design innovative products and conduct rigorous in-house testing. Recent innovations include the patent-pending Casper Core+ technology aimed at improving mattress recyclability.

Carpenter serves a diversified global marketplace, with noted customers in the medical field (where it provides tailored protection products), mattress manufacturing, transportation (including a dedicated Carpenter Transportation team), and travel and leisure sectors. The company''s domestic mattress manufacturing operations have been highlighted for supporting American jobs and local communities.

The company emphasizes its purpose, vision, mission, and values as guiding principles, alongside a code of conduct and ethics. Environmental stewardship is a stated focus, with efforts to enhance quality of life while preserving the planet.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Polyurethane foam manufacturing", "Polyether polyol production", "Polyester fiber production", "Insulation material manufacturing", "Research & development", "In-house testing", "Vertical integration"], "industries": ["Medical", "Mattress manufacturing", "Transportation", "Travel and leisure"], "materials": ["Polyurethane foam", "Polyether polyols", "Polyester fibers", "Insulation materials", "Latex foam", "Specialty polymers"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["World''s largest vertically integrated manufacturer of polyurethane foams", "More than 60 production locations globally", "6,500+ employees worldwide", "State-of-the-art R&D facilities in Richmond and beyond", "Patented Casper Core+ technology improving mattress recyclability"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1950 -> /about", "Headquartered in Moore, Oklahoma -> db", "6,500+ employees globally -> /", "World''s largest vertically integrated manufacturer of polyurethane foams -> /", "More than 60 production locations -> /", "Manufactures polyether polyols, polyester fibers, insulation materials -> /", "R&D facilities in Richmond -> /about", "Casper Core+ technology for mattress recyclability -> /", "Domestic mattress manufacturing supports American jobs -> /", "Serves medical field (tailored protection) -> industries_served", "Transportation team mentioned -> /", "Travel and leisure experiences -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Carpenter Co. is the world''s largest vertically integrated manufacturer of polyurethane foams", "founded_year": "1950", "employee_count": "6500", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='carpenter-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Catamount Solar, based in Randolph, Vermont, was established in 2011 as a worker-owned cooperative. The company began with a mission to help families, farms, and businesses reduce dependence on fossil-fuel energy through solar power. Ownership is structured as a member-owned cooperative where all workers are either members or on a track to become member-owners.

The cooperative designs and installs solar power systems for residential, commercial, off-grid, and battery backup applications. Its technicians bring decades of combined experience to each project, handling system design, installation, and ongoing service. The company does not disclose facility size or headcount, but emphasizes that employee ownership leads to low turnover and a stable, experienced installation crew.

Catamount Solar serves residential homeowners, agricultural operations, commercial businesses, and institutional clients such as schools. Notable projects include installations for Crossett Brook Middle School in Duxbury, and residential systems for customers in Woodstock and Thetford. The company works with clients of all sizes seeking energy independence and cost savings.

The cooperative model is central to its differentiation: employee-owners share profits through patronage dividends and participate in governance. Catamount Solar donates 5% of annual profits to Vermont community organizations. The ownership structure is intended to ensure long-term warranty support and continuity, as the company is less likely to be sold.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar power system design", "Solar panel installation", "Residential solar installation", "Commercial solar installation", "Off-grid solar system design and installation", "Battery backup system installation", "Solar system service and maintenance"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Agricultural", "Educational"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vermont''s only employee-owned solar company", "Worker-owned cooperative with profit sharing and democratic governance", "Donates 5% of annual profits to local community organizations", "Low employee turnover resulting in highly experienced installation crews", "Ownership structure designed to guarantee long-term warranty support"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2011 -> /about-us", "Employee-owned worker''s cooperative -> /about-us, /", "Headquarters in Randolph, Vermont -> db", "Services: residential, commercial, off-grid, battery backup solar installation -> /", "Donates 5% of profits to community organizations -> /about-us", "Customer examples: Crossett Brook Middle School, Denise Lyons & Michael Stoner, Paul McGovern -> /", "Vermont''s only employee-owned solar company -> /about-us", "Low turnover, experienced installers -> /about-us", "Long-term warranty support due to ownership structure -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Catamount Solar is a local, member-owned worker\u2019s cooperative specializing in affordable, high-quality solar power system design and installation services.", "founded_year": "2011", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Employee-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='catamount-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Central Carolina Products, Inc. operates from Burlington, North Carolina, where it was founded in 1993 as a minority-owned, family-operated business.

The company specializes in custom injection molding of thermoplastics using 61 microprocessor-controlled presses ranging from 40 to 1,650 tons. Its capabilities extend to scientific molding (RJG/Kistler), insert and over molding, hot oil molding, and sequential valve gate control, complemented by robotic extraction, custom end-of-arm tooling, and automated material handling. Value-added services include assembly, decorative coating, design and development support, tool construction and repair, and laboratory validation testing.

Primary customers are automotive OEMs and tier suppliers — General Motors, Lear Corporation, IAC, and Tower Components appear in testimonials — along with industrial manufacturers such as Stanley Black & Decker and Xylem. The firm is registered to ISO 9001:2015 and NSF/ANSI 61, and follows AIAG quality standards.

Central Carolina Products positions itself as a single-source provider, combining molding, finishing, and assembly under one roof in a climate-controlled environment. The company emphasizes engineering collaboration, process capability (CPK) monitoring, and APQP/PPAP compliance as differentiators rooted in its founding goal to deliver dimensionally critical and cosmetically perfect parts.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','NSF/ANSI 61']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom injection molding", "Insert molding", "Over molding", "Hot oil molding", "Sequential valve gate control", "Scientific molding (RJG/Kistler)", "Robotic extraction", "Custom end-of-arm tooling", "Automated material handling", "Silo material storage", "Assembly", "Decorative coating", "Design & development support", "Tool construction & repair", "Engineering change support", "Advanced Product Quality Planning (APQP)", "Production Part Approval Process (PPAP)", "Product validation laboratory testing"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Industrial"], "materials": ["Thermoplastics"], "equipment": ["Microprocessor-controlled injection molding presses (40-1,650 ton)", "RJG/Kistler scientific molding systems", "Robotic extraction systems", "Custom end-of-arm tooling", "Automated material handling systems", "Silo material storage"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Single-source molding, finishing, and assembly", "RJG/Kistler scientific molding for process control", "Climate-controlled, clean-room-grade production environment", "In-house engineering, design, and tooling support", "Minority-owned, family-operated since 1993"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1993, minority-owned, family-operated, privately held -> /about-us", "Two facilities: new plant 2003, second acquired 2008 -> /about-us", "61 presses, 40-1,650 ton range -> /services", "Scientific molding (RJG/Kistler), insert/over/hot oil molding, sequential valve gate -> /services", "Robotic extraction, custom end-of-arm t