UPDATE companies SET description='Central Metal Fabricators, Inc. (CMF) was founded in 1980 in Farmingdale, New Jersey, beginning as a welding and repair shop. Over more than four decades, the company has evolved into a full-service designer and fabricator of precision components and assemblies.

Operating from a 35,000-square-foot facility, CMF employs approximately 25 skilled personnel dedicated to design, fabrication, and assembly. The shop offers laser cutting, CNC milling, turning, punching, and bending, along with MIG and TIG welding, mechanical and electrical assembly, wire and cable manufacturing, and industrial sewing for strap assemblies. The company stocks over 800 parts and maintains documentation for thousands more, supporting both prototype and production runs.

Approximately 95 percent of CMF’s work serves the United States Armed Forces, with the remainder going to commercial, industrial, medical, pharmaceutical, research, and food-preparation sectors. The company supports major military installations including Aberdeen Proving Ground, Picatinny Arsenal, Tobyhanna Army Depot, and Naval Air Systems Command, providing replacement parts for legacy systems such as the Trojan V3 Communication Shelter and Prophet Control.

CMF emphasizes a track record of zero financial defaults, zero litigation, zero lost-time injuries, and zero adverse actions from the EPA, OSHA, or NJDEP. The firm also differentiates itself through reverse-engineering expertise for obsolete or defective parts and a commitment to traditional business values.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','AWS Certified Welding']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design and engineering", "Rapid prototyping", "Reverse engineering", "Laser cutting", "CNC milling", "CNC turning", "CNC punching", "CNC bending", "Shearing", "Pressing", "Rolling", "Forming", "MIG welding", "TIG welding", "Mechanical assembly", "Electrical assembly", "Wire and cable manufacturing", "Industrial sewing (strap manufacturing)", "Quality inspection (digital and manual)"], "industries": ["Military", "Commercial", "Industrial", "Medical", "Pharmaceutical", "Research", "Food preparation"], "materials": ["Aluminum", "Stainless steel", "Ferrous alloys", "Nonferrous alloys", "Plastics", "Exotic alloys"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Zero financial defaults in company history", "Zero litigation history", "Zero lost-time injuries", "Zero adverse regulatory actions (EPA, OSHA, NJDEP)", "Reverse engineering for obsolete/legacy parts"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1980 -> /about", "Headquarters Farmingdale, New Jersey -> /about", "Facility size 35,000 sq ft -> / and /about", "Employee count approximately 25 -> /about", "ISO 9001:2015 certification -> / and /about", "AWS Certified Welding -> / and /services", "95% services for US Armed Forces -> /about", "Industries served: commercial, industrial, military, medical, pharmaceutical, research, food preparation -> /about", "Military installations list -> /about", "Capabilities: laser cutting, CNC milling, turning, punching, bending -> /about and /services", "Materials: aluminum, stainless steel, ferrous/nonferrous alloys, plastics, exotic alloys -> /services", "Reverse