UPDATE companies SET description='Certified Parts Corporation (CPC) was founded in 1982 by James Grafft in Edgerton, Wisconsin. The company began with a mission to preserve well-known international and local legacy brands facing extinction. Grafft’s experience at Fox Corporation in Janesville, where he saw the need for continuous parts supply for defunct manufacturers, led him to purchase the service parts division when Fox shut down in 1976. He later acquired the Bridgestone brand on his 26th birthday and established CPC in 1982, acquiring the Arctic Cat snowmobile division from bankruptcy.

Today, CPC operates a 200,000-square-foot factory in Edgerton where it manufactures original service parts, including carburetors and the full line of Comet torque converters and clutches. The company acquires legacy brands—such as TecumsehPower, Comet, Hoffco, Wisconsin Wagon, and vintage recreational vehicle lines—and restarts production of their components. It also manages extensive parts inventories and provides distribution and service support through a worldwide dealer network.

CPC serves OEMs and aftermarket customers in recreational, construction, agricultural, and marine industries. Its brand portfolio includes snowmobile, mini-cycle, watercraft, and outdoor power equipment lines. Concrete examples include supplying Comet clutches to OEM manufacturers across multiple sectors and supporting engines for snowmobiles, mini-cycles, and utility equipment through the Lauson, Snow King, and LCT brands.

The company’s guiding principle is a passion for history and recognizing opportunity in orphaned brands. By acquiring intellectual property, tooling, and inventory, CPC keeps legacy products running and reintroduces historic names to the market, such as the 1895 Lauson engine line.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Service parts manufacturing", "Carburetor manufacturing", "Torque converter manufacturing", "Clutch manufacturing", "Legacy brand acquisition and revival", "OEM parts supply", "Parts inventory management", "Worldwide distribution and service network", "Licensing and joint venture management"], "industries": ["Recreational", "Construction", "Agricultural", "Marine"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Mission to preserve legacy brands facing extinction", "Major supplier to OEMs with revived historic brands", "Owns motorcycle and mini-cycle brands including Bridgestone, Indian, Rupp, Chaparral, Steen", "200,000 sq ft factory manufacturing original carburetors, torque converters, and clutches", "Worldwide service and distribution network under TecumsehPower and Comet"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1982 by James Grafft in Edgerton, WI -> /", "Mission to preserve legacy brands -> /", "Acquired Fox service parts division 1976, Bridgestone 1976 -> /", "Acquired Arctic Cat snowmobile division 1982 -> /", "200,000 sq ft factory in Edgerton manufacturing carburetors, Comet torque converters and clutches -> /", "Purchased TecumsehPower assets 2009, established Lauson Power Products -> /", "Purchased Comet drives and Hoffco assets 2009 -> /", "Comet supplies OEMs in recreational, construction, agricultural, marine -> /", "Partnership with LCT for Lauson, Snow King, LCT engines -> /", "Purchased Wisconsin Wagon 2010 -> /", "Jay Grafft promoted to President 2021 -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "original parts including carburetors and the full line of Comet torque converts and clutches are manufactured", "founded_year": "1982", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='certified-parts-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Chairmans Foods LLC operates from Nashville, Tennessee, producing premium prepared foods for foodservice and retail channels. The company does not publicly disclose its founding year or ownership structure, and no founders are named in available materials.

The company specializes in high-quality entrées, main dishes, sides, soups, queso, and other comfort foods. It maintains hundreds of proven recipes and a proprietary product development process, offering custom production of bulk recipes and exact duplication of proprietary products at national scale. Facility size, headcount, and annual volumes are not disclosed.

Chairmans Foods serves foodservice operators and retail stores, including restaurants and retail customers seeking consistent, high-quality prepared foods that reduce labor and operating costs. Its brands are designed for both consumer and restaurant channels.

