UPDATE companies SET description='Champlain Cable Corporation was founded in 1946 in Plattsburgh, New York. The company began as a manufacturer of copper and aluminum wire and tubing for building and refrigeration applications.

Today, Champlain Cable designs and manufactures high-performance wire and cable solutions using electron beam cross-linking, custom polymer compounds, and advanced insulation systems. The company operates with 50 to 199 employees and maintains in-house irradiation, testing, research and development, and custom engineering capabilities. Its product portfolio includes branded lines such as EXAR, EXRAD, EXRAD Rail, DATACLEAR, and DATARAD, serving applications from automotive and rail to military shipboard communications.

Customers include OEMs, Tier 1 suppliers, and government agencies such as the U.S. Navy, for which Champlain Cable developed QPL-accepted DATACLEAR data cables for shipboard use. A distribution partnership with Cameron Connect provides quick-turn access to EXRAD-Rail products for the North American rail transit market.

