UPDATE companies SET description='Champlain Metals was founded in 2004 by John Marius in Burlington, Vermont. Marius, who trained with the French artisans'' guild Compagnons du Devoir, brought metalworking traditions from the Champagne and Alsatian regions of France and the New York metropolitan area to the Champlain Valley.

The shop provides design, custom fabrication, casting, and forging for structural and ornamental metalwork. Its output ranges from architectural elements such as stair stringers, bronze cap rails, and awning brackets to finished goods like garden trowels, side tables, and heat exchangers.

