UPDATE companies SET description='Cherrywood Hand Dyed Fabrics operates from Baxter, Minnesota, where it was founded in 1991 by Dawn Hall.

Its product line includes solid and gradation color cards, quilt patterns, and a monthly subscription program called Monthly Color Infusion featuring unique colors, dye experiments, and overdyes. Operations run from a Minnesota studio that opens to visitors two days a week.

Cherrywood serves quilters, garment makers, and home decor enthusiasts through direct online sales and community events. Its fabrics appear in art quilt challenges such as the annual Jane Goodall Challenge and the Poppy Challenge exhibit shown at the Festival of Quilts in Birmingham, England. The company also partners with organizations for cancer awareness initiatives like Sew Pink.

