UPDATE companies SET description='Chicana Foods is based in Boise, Idaho. The company was founded by first-generation Mexican-American professional photographer Allison Corona with the help of her sisters Claudia and Giovanna and their mother, Gloria. The venture draws on family recipes from Mexico, where the founders'' maternal aunts and uncles have operated a salsa business for over two decades.

The company produces salsa macha, a traditional condiment from the Veracruz and Oaxaca regions, using high-quality seeds, nuts, chiles, olive oil, and dried fruit. The recipe was originally developed by an aunt in Mexico and refined in Chicana Foods'' Boise kitchen.

Products are sold through a network of independent retailers across Idaho and Utah, including coffee shops such as Flying M Coffee House and Common Ground Coffee, specialty grocers like Idaho Made and Hillfort Farm, farmers markets such as The RealEx Stand, gift shops like Teal Magnolia Gifts, and wine tasting rooms including Indian Creek Winery.

