UPDATE companies SET description='Cirtec Medical is based in Brooklyn Park, Minnesota.

The company develops and manufactures Class II and III medical devices with a focus on advanced catheter technologies. Its capabilities span precision extrusion, braiding, coiling, delivery sheath systems, and laser processing for catheter shafts. In precision metals, it offers micron-level CNC machining, Swiss milling, and laser welding, cutting, and marking for intricate metal components. Its microelectronics division leverages three decades of experience in thin-film technology, custom ASICs, and flexible electronics for implantable and wearable systems. Additional expertise includes silicone and synthetic polyisoprene molding for implantable devices, drug delivery, and medical tubing. Cirtec integrates design, development, and manufacturing under one roof to accelerate time to market.

Cirtec serves the medical device industry, with specific focus on neurovascular, structural heart, electrophysiology, and cardiovascular applications. Its customers include medical device companies seeking minimally invasive solutions for complex anatomies. The company also supports neurostimulation, drug delivery, and wearable medical system markets.

Cirtec differentiates itself through integrated end-to-end capabilities that reduce handoffs and risk, a quality system built for Class III devices, and proprietary platforms such as the ACCEL+ neurostimulation platform and the Navigator catheter handle platform. Its microelectronics heritage enables miniaturization and reliability in implantable systems.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Precision extrusion", "Braiding", "Coiling", "Delivery sheath systems", "Laser processing (welding, cutting, marking)", "Micron-level CNC machining", "Swiss milling", "High-speed stamping", "Complex medical extrusions", "Thin-film technology", "Custom ASIC development", "Flexible electronics manufacturing", "Balloon forming", "Electrode integration", "Silicone molding", "Synthetic polyisoprene processing", "Microelectronics assembly", "PCB assembly", "Catheter subassembly", "Design and development", "Quality management system (Class III)", "Regulatory support"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Neurovascular", "Structural heart", "Electrophysiology", "Cardiovascular", "Implantable devices", "Drug delivery", "Wearable medical systems", "Neurostimulation"], "materials": ["Biocompatible metals", "Silicone", "Synthetic polyisoprene", "Medical-grade polymers for extrusion", "Thin-film materials", "ASIC substrates", "Flexible electronics substrates"], "equipment": ["CNC machining centers (micron-level)", "Swiss milling machines", "Laser welding, cutting, and marking systems", "High-speed stamping presses", "Extrusion lines for complex medical profiles", "Braiding machines", "Coiling equipment", "Balloon forming equipment", "Thin-film deposition systems", "Silicone molding equipment", "Synthetic polyisoprene processing equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "Micron-level precision", "built_on": ["Integrated design, development, and manufacturing from concept to commercialization", "Three decades of microelectronics and thin-film expertise", "Proprietary ACCEL+ neurostimulation and Navigator catheter handle platforms", "Micron-level precision for Class II and III medical devices", "Quick-turn complex extrusions for cardiovascular and neurovascular applications"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Brooklyn Park, Minnesota -> db", "Specializes in advanced catheter technologies: precision extrusion, braiding, coiling, delivery sheath systems, laser processing -> db", "Offers precision metals: micron-level CNC machining, Swiss milling, laser welding/cutting/marking -> /", "Provides advanced electronics: thin-film technology, custom ASICs, flexible electronics, three decades of expertise -> /", "Develops advanced catheter technologies: braiding, balloon forming, electrode integration -> /", "Works with silicone and synthetic polyisoprene for implantable devices, drug delivery, medical tubing -> /", "Serves neurovascular, structural heart, electrophysiology, cardiovascular markets -> db, /", "Customers include leading medical device companies -> /", "Integrated design, development, manufacturing reduces handoffs and risk -> /", "Quality system for Class III devices -> /", "Proprietary platforms: ACCEL+ neurostimulation, Navigator catheter handle -> /", "Quick-turn complex extrusions for cardiovascular and neurovascular applications -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Delivering precision, quality, and efficiency in medical device innovation through expert-driven design, development, and manufacturing.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='cirtec-medical' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
